Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] feat(studio): hide the GitHub surfaces when the platform
 has no GitHub App

Studio opens the GitHub App of Supabase (lib/github.ts) for every
GitHub button, and shows the GitHub card, the Connections row of the
account preferences and the "Sync with a GitHub branch" block of the
branch dialogs on every platform. A platform run by someone else has
no App of Supabase's to offer: the buttons lead to an App the platform
cannot receive webhooks from, and the pages read as if the user were
connected.

Add the feature key integrations:github (default true, like
integrations:vercel). The platform lists it in disabled_features while
it has no GitHub App, and Studio then hides the GitHub section of the
project and organization integration settings, the Connections section
of the account preferences, the GitHub status of the Branches side
menu and the GitHub block of the create and edit branch dialogs.
